## What this project is

`{{projectName}}` is a Strapi {{strapiVersion}} project, {{#if isExisting}}Dockerized with{{else}}scaffolded and Dockerized by{{/if}} [dockphine](https://github.com/dockphine/dockphine). It runs as a set of Docker containers rather than a bare Node process — treat Docker as the primary way to run, build, and reason about this project.

## Stack

- Strapi {{strapiVersion}} (headless CMS)
- Database: {{dbEngine}}{{#unless (eq dbEngine "sqlite")}} (running in its own `db` container){{/unless}}
- Runs on port {{port}} inside the `strapi` container

## Docker layout

- `Dockerfile` — multi-stage build. The `build` stage installs dependencies and runs `strapi build`; the `production` stage is the slim runtime image that actually ships.
- `docker-compose.yml` — defines the `strapi` service{{#unless (eq dbEngine "sqlite")}} and the `db` service ({{dbEngine}}){{/unless}}. This is the source of truth for how the app runs locally.
- `.dockerignore` — keeps `node_modules`, `.git`, and secrets out of the build context.

## Secrets — read this before touching env files

- `.env` holds the REAL secrets (APP_KEYS, JWT_SECRET, ADMIN_JWT_SECRET, API_TOKEN_SALT, TRANSFER_TOKEN_SALT, ENCRYPTION_KEY, database credentials). It is gitignored. Do not commit it, do not print its contents, and do not regenerate these values casually — rotating them invalidates existing Strapi admin sessions and API tokens.
- `.env.example` is committed and holds fake, correctly-shaped placeholder values plus a warning comment. It is documentation, not configuration — never copy real secrets into it.

## Running it locally

```
docker compose up --build
```

Strapi admin panel: http://localhost:{{port}}/admin

